  {
   "type": "note",
   "x": 0,
   "y": 66,
   "w": 760,
   "h": 202,
   "title": "CONCEPT",
   "text": "Full rebuild of the Delphine b-roll library killing the 3D-render look. Every frame is generated FROM a real reference frame (real TikTok/IG footage, or Brooks's own iPhone photos of the AG 25cm) \u2014 the seed supplies lighting, camera, grain and composition; the product refs supply geometry only. Every scene passed the situational-awareness test (nameable moment), product-truth QA (turn-lock block, horizontal straps to side roller buckles, black interior lining), capacity law (no phone/sunglasses in flatlays), and a numeric leather-warmth check. 49 stills across street/cafe/car/home/packing/open-bag/flatlay/macro. APPROVE HERE, then animation runs on Omni with constant-distance HOLD motions only (no push-ins \u2014 they inflate this 25cm bag).",
   "color": "#f7f5ee",
   "id": "c002"
  },
